  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through next Thursday)\nIssued at 1229 PM CDT Fri Sep 18 2026\n\nA wetter and cooler weather pattern is anticipated for next week but \nwith a high degree of uncertainty. The upper level ridge will be \nfurther suppressed early next week with a series of short wave \ntroughs moving across the Central Plains. A cold front will approach \nthe area on Sunday but looks to stall out in the Texas Panhandle \nleading to at least one more very warm day. The departing short wave \ntrough may be slower than anticipated keeping at least some large \nscale ascent off the caprock on Sunday afternoon with subsidence \nswinging overhead on the caprock. Models are then aggressive in \nresuming the push of the cold front through the area early Monday \nmorning finally bringing temperatures closer to seasonal averages. \nThe resultant low level upslope flow for several days may bring an \nextended period of wet conditions for the first half of next week.",
